     "text": "================================================================================\n          60-SECOND RAPID-FIRE FOURIER SERIES PROBLEM SOLVER (GATE)\n================================================================================\n\n[START: Given Periodic Signal x(t) with Period T_0]\n   \u2502\n   \u251c\u2500\u25ba STEP 1: Verify Periodicity & Commensurability\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500 If x(t) = x_1(t) + x_2(t): Check T_1 / T_2 \\in \\mathbb{Q}\n   \u2502     \u2502    \u251c\u2500 No  \u2500\u2500\u25ba STOP: Signal is APERIODIC. No CTFS exists!\n   \u2502     \u2502    \u2514\u2500 Yes \u2500\u2500\u25ba T_0 = LCM(T_1, T_2), \\omega_0 = 2\\pi / T_0.\n   \u2502     \u2514\u2500 Identify \\omega_0 = 2\\pi / T_0.\n   \u2502\n   \u251c\u2500\u25ba STEP 2: Evaluate DC Component c_0 via Area\n   \u2502     \u2514\u2500 c_0 = (Net Geometric Area over one T_0) / T_0\n   \u2502          \u251c\u2500 Triangular: 0.5 * base * height\n   \u2502          \u251c\u2500 Rectangular: width * height\n   \u2502          \u2514\u2500 Sinusoidal lobe: (2 / \\pi) * Peak * (T_0 / 2)\n   \u2502\n   \u251c\u2500\u25ba STEP 3: Waveform Symmetry Scan (Instant Coefficient Zeroing)\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Check Half-Wave Symmetry: x(t + T_0/2) == -x(t)?\n   \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500 YES \u2500\u2500\u25ba c_0 = 0, ALL EVEN HARMONICS ARE ZERO (c_{2k} = 0).\n   \u2502     \u2502                Active harmonics: n = \\pm 1, \\pm 3, \\pm 5, ...\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Check Even Symmetry: x(-t) == x(t)?\n   \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500 YES \u2500\u2500\u25ba b_n = 0. All coefficients are purely real: c_n \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n   \u2502     \u2502                If also HWS (EQWS) \u2500\u2500\u25ba ONLY ODD COSINE terms exist!\n   \u2502     \u2502                Use a_n = (8/T_0) \\int_0^{T_0/4} x(t) cos(n\\omega_0 t) dt.\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Check Odd Symmetry: x(-t) == -x(t)?\n   \u2502           \u2514\u2500 YES \u2500\u2500\u25ba a_n = 0, c_0 = 0. All coefficients are purely imaginary: c_n \\in j\\mathbb{R}.\n   \u2502                      If also HWS (OQWS) \u2500\u2500\u25ba ONLY ODD SINE terms exist!\n   \u2502                      Use b_n = (8/T_0) \\int_0^{T_0/4} x(t) sin(n\\omega_0 t) dt.\n   \u2502\n   \u251c\u2500\u25ba STEP 4: Choose Computational Pipeline\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500 Piecewise Linear / Continuous Waveform?\n   \u2502     \u2502    \u2514\u2500\u25ba USE DOUBLE-DERIVATIVE IMPULSE SHORTCUT:\n   \u2502     \u2502          x''(t) = \\sum_k \\Delta s_k \\delta(t - t_k)\n   \u2502     \u2502          c_n = [ -1 / (n^2 \\omega_0^2 T_0) ] * \\sum_k \\Delta s_k e^{-j n \\omega_0 t_k}\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500 Piecewise Constant / Square / Step Waveform?\n   \u2502     \u2502    \u2514\u2500\u25ba USE SINGLE-DERIVATIVE IMPULSE SHORTCUT:\n   \u2502     \u2502          x'(t) = \\sum_k \\Delta x_k \\delta(t - t_k)\n   \u2502     \u2502          c_n = [ 1 / (j n \\omega_0 T_0) ] * \\sum_k \\Delta x_k e^{-j n \\omega_0 t_k}\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u2514\u2500 Linear Combination of Standard Sinusoids?\n   \u2502          \u2514\u2500\u25ba USE EULER EXPANSION:\n   \u2502                cos(\\omega t) = (e^{j\\omega t} + e^{-j\\omega t})/2\n   \u2502                sin(\\omega t) = (e^{j\\omega t} - e^{-j\\omega t})/(2j)\n   \u2502                Direct inspection: Match coefficients with \\sum c_n e^{j n \\omega_0 t}.\n   \u2502\n   \u251c\u2500\u25ba STEP 5: Power & LTI Response Query\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500 Harmonic Power Query at \\omega = n \\omega_0?\n   \u2502     \u2502    \u2514\u2500\u25ba Physical power = 2 |c_n|^2 = (1/2) C_n^2 = (1/2)(a_n^2 + b_n^2).\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500 Total Average Power Query?\n   \u2502     \u2502    \u2514\u2500\u25ba Time domain: P_avg = (1/T_0) \\int_{T_0} x^2(t) dt.\n   \u2502     \u2502\n   \u2502     \u2514\u2500 LTI System Filtering Query?\n   \u2502          \u2514\u2500\u25ba Output coefficients: d_n = c_n * H(j n \\omega_0).\n   \u2502              Output power: P_y = \\sum |c_n|^2 |H(j n \\omega_0)|^2.\n   \u2502\n   \u2514\u2500\u25ba STEP 6: Convergence at Discontinuity Query\n         \u2514\u2500\u25ba Value at jump t_d = [ x(t_d^+) + x(t_d^-) ] / 2 (Midpoint rule).\n             Gibbs overshoot = 8.95% of step height (Persistent, does not vanish).\n================================================================================"
